    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS\nintroduces another \"first\" in\nair travel comfort...\n*\nThe\nSleeperette\ncompartment\nPAA\n• a luxurious new travel unit\nwith day and night comfort\n• exclusively for trans-Pacific\npassengers on the world-famous\nFLYING CLIPPERS\n* Patent applied for",
      "EXPERIENCE THAT COUNTS\nIN CROSSING THE WORLD'S\nLARGEST OCEAN\nHere's real take-it-easy comfort! Pan American's\nSleeperettes look more comfortable ... really are more\ncomfortable than ordinary seating. You sink right into\nthe soft, luxurious, foam-rubber cushions. The curved\nheadrest comfortably supports your head.\nLike a little social get-\ntogether? Then ask\nyour neighbors to join\nyou. Sleeperette seats can\nbe turned around to face\neach other. It's ideal for\nfamily groups or game\nenthusiasts.\nThe fold-away table\n(with a reading rack) can\nbe adjusted for cards and\nother games, for reading,\nwriting or office work\nsuch as typing; and busy\nexecutives have \"office\"\nprivacy at any time.\nPioneer in the Pacific. In the 19 years since Pan American pio-\nneered over-ocean transport, Flying Clippers have flown over\n6 million passengers more than half-a-billion overseas miles.\nThat's equivalent to more than 71,000 Pacific crossings. First\nairline to span this vast ocean (1935), Pan American today\nserves the entire Pacific Basin.\nPioneer in service, too. In establishing the world's longest com-\nmercial\nairlanes, Pan\nAmerican developed many important\ntrans-ocean services... including long-range weather forecast-\ning, improved radio equipment, instrument flying and advanced\naerial navigation. Many other services have been introduced by\nPan American --from in-flight meals to steward service. And\nnow, the Sleeperette.\nTime-tested equipment. Big, 4-engine Clippers serve you in the\nPacific. Douglas DC-4s that took the greatest flight test in the\nhistory of aviation. Logging millions of miles under grueling\nwartime conditions, the Douglas DC-4 was rated perfect for\nperformance, safety and durability.\nBest - trained personnel. Your pilot? He's gone through the\nworld's most rigid training! He has averaged more than 1½\nmillion miles in the air. He's the world's most experienced\nover-ocean pilot. And he captains a seasoned multiple crew-\na vital safety factor.\nMighty handy at\nmealtime - this ad-\njustable table. There's\nno balancing of tray on\nlap. It adds to the enjoy-\nment of the delicious\nmeals and light snacks\nserved aloft... and that\ngoes for beverages from\nthe bar, too.\nWORLD -WIDE SAFETY RECORD\nFor logging 43,878,591 flying miles\nwithout a single flight accident, Pan\nAmerican now holds the coveted\nAviation Safety Award for 1946.\nAviation Safely Award\nSate-American Safely toneil.le\nPAN AMERICAN WORLO AIRWA\nAfter meals you can lean back, stretch out your legs\nfor restful relaxation, and ride through the skies- at\npeace with the world. With Sleeperette comfort, great\ndistances in the Pacific become pleasant, easy hops.\nAgent for\nPAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS\nThe System of the Hlying Clippers\nWORLD'S MOST EXPERIENCED AIRLINE\nLithographed in U.S.A.\nP35-7\nCopyright 1947, Pan American Airways, Inc.\n1998.139.018"
    ],
